# The project-hook implementations this fleet expects on a provisioned machine.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE DECLARATION, AND IT HAS TO BE ONE.
#
# The installer and the provisioning check both derived their expected set from
# what they FOUND — the installer globbed *.sh in the source directory, the
# check took the union of the manifest and the destination directory. Both then
# reported a machine missing an implementation entirely as "complete", because a
# smaller set was indistinguishable from a smaller expectation. A deleted
# implementation in core would have published a smaller set in silence.
#
# An expected set discovered from the artifacts cannot detect a missing
# artifact. It has to be declared somewhere that does not shrink when the thing
# it describes goes missing, and this is that place — read by
# install-project-hooks.sh and by provisioning-check.sh, so the two cannot
# disagree about what "provisioned" means.
#
# One hook name per line, without the .sh. Blank lines and # comments ignored.

database-sentinel
normalize-claude-md
